#subtitle: Azaña's reforms and the Africanista officer corps.

= Military Policy

The Spanish Army's officer corps is a deeply <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> institution, top-heavy with officers from the colonial wars in Morocco - the *Africanistas* - who resent both the Republic and any hint of civilian reform. Azaña, as War Minister, has already begun retiring surplus officers on full pay. What should we do to reform the military further?

- @increase_funding: Increase funding for the military to purchase its loyalty.
- @decrease_funding: Reduce funding for the military so we have more for social spending.
- @reform: Conduct a thorough reform of the officer corps, reducing the influence of the Africanistas and making it more hospitable to the Republic.
- @root: No change to military policy.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@increase_funding
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have the budget.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; coalition_dissent -= 1 if coalition_dissent > 0; army_loyalty += 0.07 if army_loyalty < 1; army_strength += 20; left_dissent += 5; pce_coalition_dissent += 1; west_relation -= 1; east_relation -= 1; radical_relation += 4; izq_rep_relation += 2; army_goal_psoe += 1; president_angry -= 10; economic_growth += 0.1

The officer corps and the <span style="color: #E8B23A;">Radical Party</span> are pleasantly surprised that we would increase military funding. Our membership tends to be anti-militarist, and is less enthused.

@decrease_funding
subtitle: +1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: There is nothing left to cut.
choose-if: army_strength > 0
on-arrival: budget += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist == 1; radical_relation -= 8; izq_rep_relation -= 4; ceda_relation -= 4; army_militancy -= 1; army_strength -= 20; falange_militia_strength += 15; requetes_strength += 5; falange_militia_militancy += 0.05; army_loyalty -= 0.05 if army_loyalty > 0; coup_progress += 1; coup_progress += 1 if army_loyalty < 0.2; coup_progress += 1 if army_loyalty < 0.1; coup_progress += 1 if army_loyalty <= 0; africa_army += 1; reichswehr_goal_completed = 1; army_goal_psoe += 1; president_angry += 10; economic_growth -= 0.1

The military has fewer guns and fewer soldiers. There is no hint of a coup yet, but we do not know where the line will be drawn. The <span style="color: #E8B23A;">Radicals</span> and <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CEDA**</span> are committed to the military and deeply opposed to our budget cuts.

Many demobilized soldiers and reservists have joined the right-wing militias such as the <span style="color: #2E3B6E;">**Requetés**</span> and <span style="color: #14322a;">**Falange**</span>, and weapons are missing from our stockpiles.

@reform
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1 and army_loyalty < 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget < 1 : We do not have the budget. ?][? if army_loyalty >= 1 : The Army is already fully loyal to the democratic government. ?]
on-arrival: coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist == 1; army_loyalty += 0.15; army_militancy -= 0.5 if army_loyalty < 0.5; budget -= 1; coup_progress += 1; africa_army += 2; radical_relation -= 5; pacifism += 1; democratization += 1; president_angry += 5;

Our efforts are at least somewhat successful; we have changed the recruiting and promotion patterns so that officers loyal to the Republic can advance, hopefully changing the culture of the officer corps. We have also retired more of the Africanista officers who resent civilian rule.

The <span style="color: #E8B23A;">Radicals</span> and <span style="color: #0087DC;">**CEDA**</span> are committed to the military and deeply suspicious of our efforts to reform it, and the retired Africanista officers - Sanjurjo, Mola, Franco, and others - grow more openly disloyal.
